-- title:
--   Theorem 5.5 — global convergence of e-PSG to a stationary point under KL of $h(x,y)$, linear rates for KL exponent ≤ 1/2
-- statement:
--   Consider the fractional program $\min_{x\in S} f(x)/g(x)$ on a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space $\mathcal H$, with $S$ nonempty, closed and convex and $f=f^s+f^n$, and let $(x_n)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (e-PSG) with parameters $\delta,\zeta>0$, $1-\sqrt\beta\,\zeta>0$, and $\bar\mu,\bar\kappa$ as in Step 1. Let $c$ be the constant of (14) for the parameter branch used (under (BC), $c=\ell\bar\kappa^2/(2m)+\bar\mu/(2\sqrt{mM})$; without (BC), $c=0$) and
--   $$h(x,y):=\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}+\iota_S(x)+c\|x-y\|^2 .$$
--   Suppose that
--
--   1. $\liminf_{n\to\infty}\tau_n=\bar\tau>0$;
--   2. Assumptions 1, 2 and 3 hold;
--   3. $g$ is continuously differentiable on an open set containing $S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$;
--   4. $h$ satisfies the KL property at $(\bar x,\bar x)$ for all $\bar x\in S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$;
--   5. $\{x\in S: f(x)/g(x)\le f(x_0)/g(x_0)\}$ is bounded;
--   6. there are $\varepsilon,\ell_g>0$ such that for all $x,y\in S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$ with $\|x-y\|\le\varepsilon$, $\|\nabla g(x)-\nabla g(y)\|\le\ell_g\|x-y\|$.
--
--   Then $\sum_{n=0}^\infty\|x_{n+1}-x_n\|<+\infty$ and $(x_n)$ converges to a stationary point $x_\infty$ of (P). Moreover, if $h$ satisfies the KL property with an exponent $a\le 1/2$ at $(\bar x,\bar x)$ for all $\bar x\in S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$, then there are $\gamma_1,\gamma_2>0$ and $\rho\in(0,1)$ such that for all $n\in\mathbb N$
--   $$|h(x_{n+1},x_n)-h(x_\infty,x_\infty)|\le\gamma_1\rho^n\qquad\text{and}\qquad\|x_n-x_\infty\|\le\gamma_2\rho^{n/2}.$$
--
--   This is the paper's global convergence result for e-PSG: under a KL property of the merit function, which holds for instance when $f$, $g$ and $S$ are semi-algebraic, the whole sequence of iterates converges, with finite length, to a stationary point, and linearly when the KL exponent is at most $1/2$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The run of Algorithm 1 and Assumptions 1, 2 are the published `FracPSG.Subseq.EPSG` definitions; the constant $c$ is tied to the parameter branch by $(\text{ParamsBC}\wedge c=c_{BC})\vee(\text{ParamsNoBC}\wedge c=0)$. The merit function lives on the Hilbert product `WithLp 2 (H × H)`. The KL property and the KL property with an exponent are the published `HasKLProperty` and `HasKLPropertyExp`, required at $(\bar x,\bar x)$ when $\partial_L h(\bar x,\bar x)\ne\varnothing$, since the paper defines the KL property only on $\operatorname{dom}\partial_L h$. The exponent is called $a$ because $\alpha$ is the constant of (14). The two rates share the same $\rho$ and the same limit $x_\infty$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: lim inf τₙ = τ̄ > 0 → there is τ̄ > 0 with τₙ ≥ τ̄ for all large n; reason: equivalent, since τₙ ≤ 1/δ
--   - encoding: c given in (14) → (ParamsBC … ∧ c = cBC ℓ μ̄ κ̄ m M) ∨ (ParamsNoBC μ̄ κ̄ ∧ c = 0); reason: (14) defines c separately for the two Step 1 branches; the branch and c are fixed together
--   - generalization: h satisfies the KL property (with an exponent α ≤ 1/2) at (x̄, x̄) for all x̄ ∈ S ∩ dom f → the published HasKLProperty (resp. HasKLPropertyExp with exponent a ≤ 1/2) at (x̄, x̄) for every x̄ ∈ S ∩ dom f with ∂_L h(x̄, x̄) ≠ ∅; reason: the paper defines the KL property only at points of dom ∂_L h (p. 6); read literally, its hypothesis also asks ∂_L h(x̄, x̄) ≠ ∅ at every such point, which the Lean does not; the Lean hypothesis is implied by the printed one, and every cluster point (x̄, x̄) of the iterates has 0 ∈ ∂_L h(x̄, x̄)
--   - encoding: H × H and the pair (x, y) → WithLp 2 (H × H), the Hilbert product with ‖(x, y)‖² = ‖x‖² + ‖y‖²; reason: the product of two Hilbert spaces, on which the KL property is defined
--   - encoding: |h(xₙ₊₁, xₙ) − h(x∞, x∞)| → absolute difference of the real values (EReal.toReal) of h; reason: both values are finite: xₙ₊₁ and x∞ lie in S ∩ dom f
--   - generalization: g: H → (−∞, +∞] proper lower semicontinuous on H (problem (P), p. 1) → g : H → ℝ, positive on S and continuous on an open set containing S (published Assumption2), with no lower semicontinuity away from S; reason: only the values of g on a neighbourhood of S enter the algorithm and the conclusion; an extended-real g of the paper is finite and continuous near S, so it agrees there with a real-valued g of the Lean, and lower semicontinuity off S is never used (same convention as the published Theorem 4.5 items)
-- source:
--   Boţ, Dao, Li, Extrapolated Proximal Subgradient Algorithms for Nonconvex and Nonsmooth Fractional Programs, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 18, Theorem 5.5 (proof pp. 18–20)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_LimitingSubdiff
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_StandingAssumptions
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_ADMMKL_KLProperty
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_Basic
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_EPSG
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Basic
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Supplement_Stationary
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Supplement_Assumption3
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Supplement_Merit

open Filter Topology
open scoped InnerProductSpace

namespace FracPSG.Abstract.Supplement

open NonconvexSplitting.Shared NonconvexSplitting.ADMMKL FracPSG.Subseq FracPSG.Abstract

/-- Theorem 5.5 (Global convergence; Boţ–Dao–Li, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 18). Let `(xₙ)` be a run
of Algorithm 1 (problem (P) with `S` nonempty closed convex, Step 1 parameters, `x₋₁ = x₀`) with
`liminf τₙ = τ̄ > 0` (here: `τₙ ≥ τ̄ > 0` eventually), under Assumptions 1, 2 and 3, with `g`
continuously differentiable on an open set containing `S ∩ dom f`, the merit function
`h(x, y) = f(x)/g(x) + ι_S(x) + c‖x − y‖²` (`c` the constant of (14) for the run's parameter branch)
having the KL property at `(x̄, x̄)` for every `x̄ ∈ S ∩ dom f` with `∂_L h(x̄, x̄) ≠ ∅`, the sublevel
set `{x ∈ S : f(x)/g(x) ≤ f(x₀)/g(x₀)}` bounded, and `∇g` locally Lipschitz on `S ∩ dom f` in the
printed sense. Then `∑ ‖xₙ₊₁ − xₙ‖ < +∞` and `(xₙ)` converges to a stationary point `x_∞` of (P).
Moreover, if `h` has the KL property with an exponent `a ≤ 1/2` at all those `(x̄, x̄)`, there are
`γ₁, γ₂ > 0` and `ρ ∈ (0, 1)` with `|h(xₙ₊₁, xₙ) − h(x_∞, x_∞)| ≤ γ₁ρⁿ` and
`‖xₙ − x_∞‖ ≤ γ₂ρ^{n/2}` for all `n`. -/
theorem theorem_5_5
    {N : ℕ} {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N))}
    {fs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {fn : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → EReal}
    {g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar : ℝ}
    {x gs : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N)} {τ κ μ : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hS : IsClosed S) (hSconv : Convex ℝ S)
    (hA1 : Assumption1 S fs fn ℓ) (hA2 : Assumption2 S g β)
    (hδ : 0 < δ) (hζ : 0 < ζ) (hβζ : 0 < 1 - Real.sqrt β * ζ) {m M c : ℝ}
    (hpar : (ParamsBC S (objF fs fn) g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar m M ∧ c = cBC ℓ μbar κbar m M) ∨
      (ParamsNoBC μbar κbar ∧ c = 0))
    (hrun : IsEPSGRun S fs fn g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar x gs τ κ μ)
    (hτ : ∃ τbar : ℝ, 0 < τbar ∧ ∀ᶠ n in atTop, τbar ≤ τ n)
    (hA3 : Assumption3 S fs fn g)
    (hgC1 : ∃ O : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N)), IsOpen O ∧
      (∀ y ∈ S, objF fs fn y ≠ ⊤ → y ∈ O) ∧ ContDiffOn ℝ 1 g O)
    (hKL : ∀ xbar ∈ S, objF fs fn xbar ≠ ⊤ →
      (LimitingSubdiff (merit S (objF fs fn) g c) (pair xbar xbar)).Nonempty →
      HasKLProperty (merit S (objF fs fn) g c) (pair xbar xbar))
    (hS0 : Bornology.IsBounded (S0 S (objF fs fn) g (x 0)))
    (hgradLip : ∃ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε ∧ ∃ ℓg : ℝ, 0 < ℓg ∧
      ∀ y ∈ S, objF fs fn y ≠ ⊤ → ∀ y' ∈ S, objF fs fn y' ≠ ⊤ → ‖y - y'‖ ≤ ε →
        ‖gradient g y - gradient g y'‖ ≤ ℓg * ‖y - y'‖) :
    ∃ xinf : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N),
      Summable (fun n => ‖x (n + 1) - x n‖) ∧
      Tendsto x atTop (𝓝 xinf) ∧ IsStationary (objF fs fn) g S xinf ∧
      ∀ a : ℝ, a ≤ 1 / 2 →
        (∀ xbar ∈ S, objF fs fn xbar ≠ ⊤ →
          (LimitingSubdiff (merit S (objF fs fn) g c) (pair xbar xbar)).Nonempty →
          HasKLPropertyExp (merit S (objF fs fn) g c) (pair xbar xbar) a) →
        ∃ γ₁ : ℝ, 0 < γ₁ ∧ ∃ γ₂ : ℝ, 0 < γ₂ ∧ ∃ ρ : ℝ, 0 < ρ ∧ ρ < 1 ∧
          ∀ n : ℕ,
            |(merit S (objF fs fn) g c (pair (x (n + 1)) (x n))).toReal -
                (merit S (objF fs fn) g c (pair xinf xinf)).toReal| ≤ γ₁ * ρ ^ n ∧
            ‖x n - xinf‖ ≤ γ₂ * ρ ^ ((n : ℝ) / 2) := by sorry

end FracPSG.Abstract.Supplement
